{
  "title": "Synovitis of 2nd MTP",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7016/synovitis-of-2nd-mtp",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 7 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Synovitis of 2nd MTP is the most frequent monoarticular synovitis of the MTP joint frequently associated with elongated 2nd metatarsal or a hallux valgus deformity.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with tenderness plantarly over 2nd MTP plantar plate or over dorsal capsule. MRI can be helpful in cases of unclear diagnosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a trial of conservative management with shoe modifications and NSAIDs. Surgical management is indicated for patients with progressive symptoms who fail nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elongated second metatarsal relative to the first metatarsal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Morton Foot**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "hallux valgus deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "synovitis causes the capsuloligamentous apparatus of the MTP joint to become stretched",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "stretching leads to instability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "instability leads to deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "attenuation of plantar plate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "extension of MTP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sagittal plane deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "associated with cross-over toe deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "MTP instability can lead to **dorsal dislocation of MTP joint**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "predisposition to **hammer toe** deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Cadaveric cross section of plantar plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7016/images/plantar%20plate.jpg",
              "caption": "cadaver cross section showing anatomy at MTP joint"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI of plantar plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7016/images/mri%20plantar%20plate.jpg",
              "caption": "MRI of MTP joint"
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "warm joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fullness of joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain and tenderness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may have pain in second web space",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tenderness may be worse plantarly over **plantar plate** or over **dorsal capsule**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "caused by inflammation or extrinsic pressure on interdigital nerve",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pain with range of motion decreased with traction",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "global swelling of MTP",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "decreased **plantar flexion**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "deformity & motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "deformity is often passively correctable in the predislocation stages",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "instability, if present, can be demonstrated with the **dorsal drawer test**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "if able to dorsally sublux then attenuation of plantar plate present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "as deformity progresses second toe may cross over adjacent toe in a varus or valgus deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "disruption of a collateral ligament and the plantar plate",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**\"cross over toe deformity\"**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "weight-bearing AP and lateral views of foot",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "widening or medial-lateral joint space imbalance of second MTP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "dorsal subluxation of MTP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may appear like joint space narrowing or overlapping of the proximal phalanx on distal metatarsal head",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "varus or valgus deformity of toe",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "if diagnosis unclear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "quantify the extent of plantar plate or ligamentous disruption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Morton's neuroma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may mimic Mortons neuroma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "important to differentiate MTP synovitis from interdigital neuroma because a steroid injection into the interdigital space may weaken the capsuloligamentous structures at MTP joint leading to progressive deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "activity/shoe wear modifications, NSAIDs, external support of MTP joint",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "external support with crossover taping or Budin-type toe splint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "nonoperative treatment should last 10 to 12 weeks",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "subsequently avoid shoes that aggravate symptoms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "synovectomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "no deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "failure of nonoperative treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "distal oblique shortening MT osteotomy (Weil procedure)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7016/images/Weil%20procedure%20-%20courtesy%20Richardson_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fixed deformity with long second metatarsal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "preserves joint",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "rebalances metatarsal cascade",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "relaxes plantar plate and rebalances alignment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "FDL-to-EDL tendon transfer (Girdlestone-Taylor) or MTP capsular release with extensor tendon lengthening",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "fixed deformity and NO long second metatarsal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "sagittal deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Vascular compromise**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "if correcting a chronic dislocation the soft tissue, including vasculature, can contract",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "stretching of the vasculature can compromise flow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "procedure may need to be reversed to save digit",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
